{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib proof of the main results of Fan, Stone, Yang and Yin, \"Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model\" (arXiv:2504.00512). The model is H_Lambda = H + Lambda, complex Hermitian case: H has D >= 2 independent N x N Wigner blocks on the diagonal, with entry laws whose moments are bounded by given constants (Assumption 1), and Lambda places a deterministic A and A* on the cyclic off-diagonal blocks. This entry contains Theorem 2.1 (delocalized regime: under ||A|| <= N^{-delta_A} and (2.4), every eigenvector puts mass 1/D + O(N^{-c}) on each block, (2.5)) and Theorem 2.5 (localized regime: the eigenvalue shift bounds (2.10), (2.11) and the comparison of the local correlation functions with those of H). Both are stated in uniform form (constants chosen before N, then every N >= N_0, every entry law with the given moment constants, every admissible A and every k) and have no hypotheses other than their parameters; no result of another work is assumed for them. The library also proves Theorem 2.2 and Theorem 2.4, each from one external input stated as an explicit hypothesis; those two are not part of this entry.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Jun Yin"
    }
